y to predict defect likelihood.\\ndf[\'complexity_interaction\'] = df[\'v(g)\'] * df[\'d\']", "# size_interaction\\n# Interaction between total operators/operands and Halstead volume.\\n# Usefulness: Reflects how structural size interacts with cognitive attributes of the code.\\ndf[\'size_interaction\'] = df[\'n\'] * df[\'v\']", "df.drop(columns=[\'locCodeAndComment\'], inplace=True)"]': 0.0071090047393364}, {'["# log_v\\n# Log-transformed Halstead volume to reduce skewness and manage outliers.\\n# Usefulness: Captures manageable differences in volume, reducing the impact of extreme values, which could indicate defect-prone modules.\\ndf[\'log_v\'] = df[\'v\'].apply(lambda x: np.log(x + 1))", "# log_effort\\n# Log-transformed Halstead effort to reduce skewness and manage outliers.\\n# Usefulness: Helps identify modules with disproportionately high effort while managing extreme values.\\ndf[\'log_effort\'] = df[\'e\'].apply(lambda x: np.log(x + 1))", "# reciprocal_d\\n# Reciprocal transformation of Halstead difficulty to address extreme values.\\n# Usefulness: Compresses high difficulty values to emphasize manageable areas of code complexity.\\ndf[\'reciprocal_d\'] = 1 / (df[\'d\'] + 1)", "# zscore_v\\n# Z-score normalized Halstead volume.\\n# Usefulness: Standardizes this feature to compare across modules of varying sizes and complexity.\\ndf[\'zscore_v\'] = (df[\'v\'] - df[\'v\'].mean()) / df[\'v\'].std()", "# complexity_difficulty_score\\n# Interaction between cyclomatic complexity and Halstead difficulty.\\n# Usefulness: Captures modules with high control flow complexity and cognitive burden, which are likely defect-prone.\\ndf[\'complexity_difficulty_score\'] = df[\'v(g)\'] * df[\'d\']", "# branch_effort\\n# Interaction between branch count and Halstead effort.\\n# Usefulness: Identifies modules where branching contributes disproportionately to cognitive effort, indicating potential defect risks.\\ndf[\'branch_effort\'] = df[\'branchCount\'] * df[\'e\']", "# volume_intelligence_interaction\\n# Interaction between Halstead volume and intelligence per line of code.\\n# Usefulness: Highlights areas of the code with high computational density and low cognitive load, reflecting effective design.\\ndf[\'volume_intelligence_interaction\'] = df[\'v\'] * (df[\'i\'] / df[\'loc\'])", "# operator_diversity\\n# Ratio of unique operators to total operators.\\n# Usefulness: Reflects the diversity of operator use, signaling complex or varied coding techniques.\\ndf[\'operator_diversity\'] = df[\'uniq_Op\'] / df[\'total_Op\']", "# operand_diversity\\n# Ratio of unique operands to total operands.\\n# Usefulness: Indicates the diversity of data variables, which is tied to modular structure and organization.\\ndf[\'operand_diversity\'] = df[\'uniq_Opnd\'] / df[\'total_Opnd\']", "# effort_density\\n# Effort normalized by lines of code.\\n# Usefulness: Highlights modules with disproportionately high cognitive effort relative to size, signaling risk areas.\\ndf[\'effort_density\'] = df[\'e\'] / df[\'loc\']", "# cumsum_effort\\n# Cumulative sum of Halstead effort.\\n# Usefulness: Tracks incremental effort across multiple modules or within the codebase, identifying areas of excessive complexity buildup.\\ndf[\'cumsum_effort\'] = df[\'e\'].cumsum()", "# rank_v\\n# Rank transformation of Halstead volume.\\n# Usefulness: Handles outliers by ranking modules based on volume, enabling better relative comparisons.\\ndf[\'rank_v\'] = df[\'v\'].rank()", "df.drop(columns=[\'locCodeAndComment\'], inplace=True)"]': 0.004739336492891044}]
